{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The component tester fits my breadboard and PCB work because it would help me identify loose parts and check them before building circuits.",
    "LEDs with resistors are useful additions to my circuit projects, and the caliper would help measure boards, clearances, and mounting dimensions."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament assumes I own and use a 3D printer, which my electronics purchases do not establish.",
    "The feeler gauge, tap kit, threaded inserts, and cutting wheels require particular tasks, sizes, or tools that I have no established need for. The case of small gloves also assumes a fit and quantity I cannot justify."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying hands-on project supplies seems to have been treated as a reason to recommend almost any workshop item.",
    "My caster purchase seems to have been stretched into an ongoing interest in furniture hardware, although it could have served a single project."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, PCB supplies, relay, and battery holder make practical circuit assembly and component checking more relevant than unrelated workshop consumables.",
    "My earlier PCB kit already included LEDs, so another assortment is less compelling than a tester that adds a useful capability. Specific compatibility and a concrete use matter before I choose specialized supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my circuit-building interests but extended them too broadly into equipment and supplies without an established use."
}"}
